Title: Barrios vs Pacquiao: Trainer Dave Coldwell on why he won't watch legend's comeback fight
Date: 2025-07-14
Firsthand information: {'Speaker': [{'Speaker': 'Dave Coldwell', 'Text': "I won't be watching Manny Pacquiao's comeback fight on Saturday.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 1, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 55}}, {'Speaker': 'Dave Coldwell', 'Text': "It feels like a shortcut. A nod to nostalgia rather than merit, and that's unfair to fighters who are working their way up properly.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 1, 'StartChar': 56, 'EndChar': 178}}, {'Speaker': 'Dave Coldwell', 'Text': "I realise that might sound harsh given he is one of the sport's all-time greats, an eight-division world champion. I have immense respect for what he achieved in his prime. He's a global icon, a true legend.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 2, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 219}}, {'Speaker': 'Dave Coldwell', 'Text': "I had a brief exchange with Mauricio Sulaiman, the WBC president, on social media about this. He wasn't pleased with my doubt but, in my view, it sets a strange precedent and undermines the fighters who have been grinding their way up the ranks, paying their dues with tough fights.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 6, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 249}}], 'Description': [{'Description': "That's the part that really shocked me when I heard of Pacquiao's return. Usually, a fighter coming back from retirement eases into the sport with tune-up fights.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 4, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 149}}, {'Description': "Not Pacquiao. He's skipping all that and going right to the front of the queue.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 5, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 64}}], 'Image': [{'ID': 'image_1', 'Caption': 'Manny Pacquiao training for his comeback'}]}
